<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Lara and Corio sit on the northern run between Geelong and the You Yangs, and a lot of the housing along that corridor went up inside the asbestos cement window. The Housing Commission started its first Corio estates in the late 1950s and finished five estates of about 2,500 houses within roughly twenty years. Next door in Norlane the same program peaked between 1951 and 1957 and had reached 2,464 Commission houses by 1976. Asbestos cement was a standard residential building material in Australia from the mid 1940s until the late 1980s, so the dates line up almost exactly.</p><p>None of that means your place definitely has asbestos in it. It means the odds are worth taking seriously, and that guessing by eye is not good enough for anyone. Nobody can identify asbestos cement by looking at it, which is why <a href="/asbestos-testing-geelong/">a sample has to go to a NATA accredited laboratory</a> before you make any decisions. Ring us before you break anything and we will put you in touch with a licensed removalist.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Lara & Corio</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Lara & Corio Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos testing and identification</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A small sample goes to a NATA accredited laboratory, so you get a written result instead of an opinion, at published rates of roughly $88 to $160 per sample. Most houses need three to eight samples, because every material counts separately: a Corio back fence, an eaves lining and a bathroom wall sheet are three samples, not one.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Asbestos fence removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Old fibro boundary fences are the most common job in the northern suburbs, and a weathered or cracked one is the version that matters. A <a href="/asbestos-fence-removal-geelong/">whole fence line</a> is well past the 10 square metre limit, so it is licensed removalist work, and published whole fence figures sit between $1,000 and $3,500.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Roof, shed and garage removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Super Six corrugated roofing and fibro garage cladding turn up on a lot of Corio and Norlane blocks, and none of it should ever be water blasted, drilled, dry swept or walked on. <a href="/asbestos-roof-removal-geelong/">Roof removal</a> is published at $40 to $120 per square metre, with a single garage around $2,500 to $5,000 and a double around $4,000 to $8,000.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Disposal and asbestos skip bins</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Asbestos is reportable priority waste in Victoria and can only go to a landfill authorised to receive it, never into a general skip or a council hard waste collection. Drysdale Landfill is the only site in the Barwon region on the EPA register, it takes small domestic loads up to a 6x4 trailer, and you need to ring (03) 5251 2935 before you drive over, as our <a href="/asbestos-disposal-geelong/">disposal page</a> explains.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
